# Optional overrides for the root docker compose (DEV ONLY). Copy to .env;
# every value below is optional and the defaults are fine for local work.
# Docs: https://aglelectronics.github.io/con-services/contributing/local-development/

# Compose profiles to start without --profile flags (den, events, learn,
# desk, tasks, tasks-dev, wiki, stats). The core services always start.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=den,events

# Whether module backends wait for Den. Default: standalone.
#   standalone  every module works on its own; pairing with Den is optional.
#   required    a module's API answers 503 den_pairing_required (its web app
#               shows "Waiting for Den") until you pair it from Den's Modules
#               page. Needs the den profile. Like the Kubernetes setup.
# Docs: https://aglelectronics.github.io/con-services/concepts/pairing/#required-or-standalone
# DEN_MODE=standalone

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather, read by events-backend (Rally
# announcements) and learn-backend (notifications). Empty: Rally records
# announcements as dry runs and Learn sends no Telegram messages. A real
# token is a secret: keep it in .env (never committed), never in Git.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#
# Dev-only catch-all (Compose / APP_ENV=development only). When both the
# token and TELEGRAM_DEV_CATCHALL_CHAT_ID are set, every module mirrors
# notices (Tasks assigns, HR/Learn email copies, Rally announcements,
# Stash Lost & Found) to that one chat or forum topic, prefixed with who
# they were for. Email still goes to Mailpit. Never set these in production.
# TELEGRAM_DEV_CATCHALL_CHAT_ID=
# TELEGRAM_DEV_CATCHALL_THREAD_ID=
#
# Intercom staff bot (Compose profile `intercom`). Prefers INTERCOM_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN;
# otherwise uses TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN. Board chat falls back to the catch-all ids.
# Only one getUpdates poller per token — keep Stash L&F Telegram off on the
# same bot while Intercom runs (or give Stash STASH_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN).
# INTERCOM_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# INTERCOM_BOARD_CHAT_ID=
# INTERCOM_BOARD_THREAD_ID=
# INTERCOM_IDEAS_THREAD_ID=

# Settings of the shared Go packages (con-services shared/go), read by module
# backends that use them. docker-compose.yml already sets the dev values:
#   APP_ENV=development        AUTH_MODE=dev and an unencrypted Den credential
#                              are only allowed with this; default production.
#   DEN_LINK_ENCRYPTION_KEY    base64 of 32 bytes; encrypts the stored Den
#                              credential. Compose sets a public dev key per
#                              module. Production: openssl rand -base64 32,
#                              from a secret manager, one per module.
#   DEN_LINK_ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS  old key during a rotation.
#   DEN_ALLOWED_HOSTS          pairing hosts when DEN_INTERNAL_URL is empty
#                              (Compose sets DEN_INTERNAL_URL, so not needed).
#   OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM=groups   OIDC_GROUP_MATCH=full   OIDC_GROUP_PREFIX=
#   GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CREDENTIALS_FILE, GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_ADMIN_EMAIL,
#   GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_DOMAIN    Google Workspace (off when all empty).
# Docs: https://aglelectronics.github.io/con-services/concepts/shared-code/#configuration-reference

# Stash: optional Lost & Found Telegram bot token (a dev test bot from
# @BotFather) and SMTP password for overdue emails. Both empty by default.
# Dev only; real installations keep them in a secret manager.
# STASH_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# STASH_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# Lets HR read Stash's role catalog (Bearer, 32+ characters, the same value
# in HR). Unset: only signed-in staff can read it. DEV ONLY if you set one.
# STASH_HR_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# Learn (profile learn). Docs:
# https://aglelectronics.github.io/con-services/modules/learn/configuration/
#   LEARN_GROUP_DIRECTORY   keycloak (default) or off (no Keycloak admin API).
#   LEARN_LINKABLE_GROUPS   groups trainers may link; default /learn/*.
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN      empty = Telegram reminders off.
# LEARN_GROUP_DIRECTORY=keycloak
# LEARN_LINKABLE_GROUPS=/learn/*
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Stats development scaffold (profile stats). Sources implement the internal
# aggregate contract documented at docs/modules/stats/api.md. The checked-in
# token default is DEV ONLY; leave sources empty for the dashboard shell.
# STATS_POLL_INTERVAL=2m
# STATS_PULL_TIMEOUT=10s
# STATS_SOURCES=desk=http://desk-backend:8080/api/internal/stats
# STATS_SERVICE_TOKEN=change-me-dev-only-stats-pull-token-32
